      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has two distinct scenarios mixed into one method with variable reuse that hurts readability. I'll split them into clearly named test methods and extract the magic delta constant.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version splits the original single test method into two clearly named methods (`testKnownGeohashEncodeAndDecode` and `testShortGeohashRoundTrip`), extracts the magic delta into a named constant `COORDINATE_DELTA`, adds descriptive Javadoc, and eliminates the confusing variable reuse — all while calling the same methods with the same arguments and expected outcomes."
